      "updated_at": "2026-05-09T16:01:37Z",
      "body": "Hi! Triaging older issues — I think this one has actually been fixed already.\n\n- The `_pytest/tmpdir.get_user()` function was updated in commit [`14d370781`](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/commit/14d370781) (\"Catch `OSError` from `getpass.getuser()` (#11875)\", Jan 2024) to also catch `OSError`. The exception list at `src/_pytest/tmpdir.py:240` now reads `except (ImportError, OSError, KeyError)`, which is exactly the gap the issue describes.\n- That fix landed in pytest 8.1.0 (Feb 2024). The reporter mentions pytest 7.4.3, so this is a \"fixed in newer release\" situation.\n\nCould the reporter retest with pytest >= 8.1? If `OSError` still leaks under a current pytest, a fresh repro on the current `main` would re-open this with a clear next step. Otherwise this should be closeable.\n\n(Disclosure: I drafted this comment with help from Claude Code while triaging stale issues; the commit and the source-line citation above were verified manually against current `main`.)\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
